-- title:
--   Unramifiedness at vertical height-one primes over cusps of the pole chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is algebraic over $\mathbb Q$, and a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$ admitting a ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb C$ carrying $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the rational $q$-expansion function field of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of the units reduction `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')`. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with uniformiser $\varpi$ generating the maximal ideal; $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the base change [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion of $j$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ characterised by: $f \in W_0$ exactly when $f \cdot y = x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ for some power series $x,y$ over $A$ whose reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ is nonzero. Let $z$ be a point of the two-chart integral model [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$), and suppose the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$. Let $y$ be a point of `XInf`, i.e. a prime ideal of the subalgebra $A_\infty(K) =$ `chartAlgInf A K j` of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$, with $\iota_\infty(y) = z$, with $y$ maximal, with $j^{-1} \in y$, and such that every $b \in A_\infty(K)$ whose image in $K$ is a nonunit of $W_0$ lies in $y$. Let $K_0$ be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), contained in $K$, an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j_0 \in K_0$ be nonzero with the same Laurent expansion as $j$; let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism $A_\infty(K_0) \to A_\infty(K)$ inducing the inclusion $K_0 \hookrightarrow K$ on underlying elements, used to view $A_\infty(K)$ as an $A_\infty(K_0)$-algebra. The conclusion: for every prime ideal $\mathfrak Q$ of $A_\infty(K)$ with $\mathfrak Q \subseteq y$, $\operatorname{ht}\mathfrak Q = 1$ and $\varpi \in \mathfrak Q$, the algebra $A_\infty(K)$ over $A_\infty(K_0)$ is unramified at $\mathfrak Q$.
--
--   This is the pole-chart statement, at a cusp lying on the branch cut out by the Gauss valuation subring $W_0$, that the integral model of the level-$q^2M'$ curve is unramified over the corresponding chart of the $\Gamma_0(M')$ model at every vertical height-one prime, i.e. every height-one prime containing the uniformiser of the base. It feeds the proof that the local rings of the fibre at such points of the pole chart are regular.
